msgid "In order to prevent arming if a script is missing (ie. SD card ejected or file corrupted) or if a script that is supposed to run once before arming and then terminate, but does not, then either, or both, of two checksum pre-arm checks can be enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:115
#: 2f48c011d0694f3aaccbf19f9a661bb4
msgid ":ref:`SCR_LD_CHECKSUM<SCR_LD_CHECKSUM>` which checks that the checksum of all loaded scripts matches this value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:116
#: ecf864bfd2ee4908be60fff45ea86879
msgid ":ref:`SCR_RUN_CHECKSUM<SCR_RUN_CHECKSUM>` which checks that the checksum of all running scripts matches this value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:118
#: f762889ea34d4da58fa6358dee4976f2
msgid "These can be set automatically when the scripts have been loaded and the desired ones running before arming, by setting the :ref:`SCR_DEBUG_OPTS<SCR_DEBUG_OPTS>` bit 5 which will compute and set these parameter's values, and then reset bit 5 automatically."
